hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"169","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: There were debts upon men in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we know of no free man sold for a debt."
"170","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik informed me, that Mu'adh ibn Jabal - one of his people, the Banu Salamah - fell heavily into debt in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did no more for his creditors than strip him of his wealth for them."
"171","Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil al-'Asqalani and Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Sufyan narrated to us, both said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik - Ibn Dawud named him 'Abd al-Rahman - that Mu'adh ibn Jabal kept borrowing until all his wealth was consumed. His creditors came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Mu'adh asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask his creditors to remit or delay, but they refused. Had they spared anyone for anyone's sake, they would have spared Mu'adh for the sake of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold all his wealth for his debt until Mu'adh was left with nothing."
"172","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with the meaning of al-Zuhri's hadith, adding: If anything remained from its price, it is shared with the creditors. Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that whoever dies with another man's goods intact in his possession, without having paid anything from its price, the owner of the goods shares with the creditors in it."
"173","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Burd, from Sulayman ibn Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man selling food adulterated with barley and said: Separate this from this and this from this, then sell each as you wish; for there is no cheating in our religion."
"174","Isma'il ibn Mas'adah al-Tunukhi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Mahan al-'Asqalani narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Makhul, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man selling wheat, mixing the good with the bad, forbade him and said: Distinguish each one separately."
"175","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade adulterating milk for sale. Abu Dawud said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim likewise narrated it from Yunus; and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Yunus, from al-Hasan, who said: 'Umar said."
"176","'Abd al-Salam ibn 'Atiq al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi narrated to me from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling a living animal for a dead one."
"177","Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling meat for a live animal."
"178","Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamadhani and Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, both said: Ibn Wahb informed us, Musa ibn Shaybah al-Hadrami informed me from Yunus ibn Yazid, from 'Umarah ibn Ghazziyyah al-Ansari, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he and Abu Bakr left Makkah migrating to Madinah, passed a shepherd of sheep; they bought from him a sheep, stipulating that its wool remain his."
"179","Ahmad ibn Sa'id and Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, al-Layth informed me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from 'Umarah ibn Ghazziyyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the same hadith."
"180","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hiring a worker without clarifying - meaning until clarifying - his wage for him."
"181","Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not sell the wool of sheep while it is on their backs, and do not sell their milk while it is in their udders."
"182","Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Umar ibn Farrukh, from Ikrimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the same meaning."
"183","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, from Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage, a dinar."
"184","al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar; Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (Then contract them in writing, if you know any good in them). He said: If you know they have a trade, and do not send them out as a burden upon people."
